<p>Shuffle a deck of cards and divide it into four packets. Pick up any packet, look at the top card, and remember it.</p>
<p>Spell out the phrase AUSTRALIAN SHUFFLE, transferring one card from the top to the bottom of the packet for each letter.</p>
<p>Now apply the phrase Down Under &#8212; put the top card <em>down</em> on the table, and the next card <em>under</em> the packet. Continue doing this until you&#8217;re holding a single card.</p>
<p>It&#8217;s the card you memorized.</p>
<p>(<a href="https://doubledeal.wordpress.com/2010/10/23/wanna-see-a-trick-2/">By Josh Jay, based on a principle discovered by Alex Elmsley.</a>)</p>
